<title>SWEDEN: Adtranz says wins 200 mln stg British order.</title>
<headline>Adtranz says wins 200 mln stg British order.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>International railway group ABB Daimler-Benz Transportation (Adtranz ) said on Wednesday it was the preferred supplier of a British train order worth 200 million sterling ($322.5 million) over 12 years. ($ = 0.620 British Pounds Sterling)  </p>
<p>Adtranz said in a statement that it was nominated to make and maintain 44 four-car electric commuter trains for Prism Rails's LTS Rail Ltd.</p>
<p>This is the rail franchise operating train services between London's Fenchurch Street and Basildon, Tilbury, Southend, Shoeburyness, Upminster and Grays.</p>
<p>The order will be placed by Derby based Porterbrook Leasing Co Ltd, Adtranz said.</p>
<p>The first trains, which will be built at Adtranz at its Derby works, will be delivered during 1999.</p>
<p>-- Belinda Goldsmith, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1045</p>
